Mune ni kazaru mae muki naose uta tte (akirame waruittte?) shinjite kure

385
00:23:57,259 --> 00:23:58,869
以上がこちらで調べた情報です。いかがですか？
So that's everything I've got so far. What do you think?

386
00:24:02,089 --> 00:24:05,149
ここは、大空警察。
And so, here she visits the Oozora Police.

387
00:24:04,269 --> 00:24:13,209
数々の難事件を解決してきた優秀な警察から、今回の事件に関するさらなる情報を得るべく、探偵は警察署を訪れていた。
With their stellar track of solving mysterious cases like this one easily, she hopes that they can give her some leads.

388
00:24:17,349 --> 00:24:19,429
バカ、アー。事件の捜査は我々プロに任せとけばいいんだよ。
I think you should leave the investigating to the professionals.

389
00:24:26,399 --> 00:24:31,999
何？被害者の服に魔力の痕跡があったって？
I mean, magical residue on the victim's clothing?

390
00:24:32,369 --> 00:24:34,659
そうダ！そんなバカな話があるか。
Yes! That is very silly!

391
00:24:35,379 --> 00:24:41,569
こいつ、次「自分自身が凶器かもしれない」とか言い出すんじゃないですか、署長。
Next, she's going to tell that SHE'S actually involved and might be the murder weapon.

392
00:24:52,926 --> 00:24:53,686
それだ！
Wait, that's it!

393
00:24:56,068 --> 00:24:56,288
こいつ今、自分が凶器だって自白した？
Did she just confess to be the murder weapon?

394
00:25:00,183 --> 00:25:01,403
よく分かんないっす。
I'm not sure.

395
00:25:01,403 --> 00:25:03,653
ボクが言ったのはただの冗談で…
What I said was just a joke...

396
00:25:04,053 --> 00:25:08,613
もしかしてボク、無意識のうちに真実をつかんではいたのか！？
Could it be that I subconsciously grasped the truth?!

397
00:25:09,493 --> 00:25:10,693
お前天才か！？
You're a genius?!

398
00:25:10,973 --> 00:25:16,583
おや、これはいよいよ事件解決になってしまうのか？
Oh my, could this possibly mean the case is solved?

399
00:25:16,993 --> 00:25:18,613
事件解決しちゃった！
I solved the case!

400
00:25:20,223 --> 00:25:23,333
違う違う、私は凶器じゃないですよ。
No, no, I'm not the murder weapon.

401
00:25:24,044 --> 00:25:26,604
異議あり！さっき自白しただろ！
Objection! You confessed just now!

402
00:25:27,274 --> 00:25:33,444
私が言いたいのは、この事件には別の古代兵器が関わっているかもしれないということ。
What I mean is, maybe another ancient weapon is involved in this case.

403
00:25:33,814 --> 00:25:35,924
だから布に魔力が残っていたんだ。
That's why magical residue was left on the cloth.

404
00:25:37,074 --> 00:25:40,494
なんだ、そういうことか…
I see, so that's how it is...

405
00:25:41,454 --> 00:25:45,064
僕が事件を解決できたと思ったのに…
And I thought I was the one who solved the case...

406
00:25:45,454 --> 00:25:46,834
まあ次がんばれよ。
Well, do better next time.

407
00:25:47,474 --> 00:25:53,734
でもなぁ、現場の近くで変なものを見たっていう報告も届いてるんだ。
But we've also gotten reports of people seeing strange things near the crime scene.

408
00:25:54,114 --> 00:26:04,514
その魔力の痕跡とかやらが超人的な力によるものだっていうなら…変な幻覚が見えた人がいるのもそいつの影響ってこと？
If those magical traces are due to superhuman power... does that mean the people seeing strange hallucinations are affected by it too?

409
00:26:05,244 --> 00:26:09,794
それはまだ分かりませんが、謎は必ず解いてみせましょう。
I'm not sure yet, but I'll definitely solve the mystery.

410
00:26:10,464 --> 00:26:12,804
じゃあうちの捜査資料を持ってっていいよ。
Then you can take our investigation files.

411
00:26:13,324 --> 00:26:15,434
民間人にあげちゃダメっすよ！
You can't give that to a civilian!

412
00:26:15,744 --> 00:26:18,514
でもこいつさぁ、なんか天才の匂いしね？
But this one here, she kind of smells like a genius, doesn't she?

413
00:26:19,434 --> 00:26:22,554
さっきはボクのこと天才って言ったじゃないですかぁ…。
You called me a genius just a moment ago...

414
00:26:22,934 --> 00:26:24,604
どんな情報でも助かりますよ。
Any information would be helpful.

415
00:26:24,964 --> 00:26:32,064
ただし！資料が欲しいなら、タダというわけにはいかんな！
However! If you want the files, it's not going to be free!

416
00:26:33,524 --> 00:26:35,974
これ、また歌う流れですか？
Are we singing again?

417
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:46,949
おれは知らない 何も知らない
I don't know anything, I know nothing at all

418
00:26:46,949 --> 00:26:49,719
何も見てない 誰も見てない
I haven't seen anything, nobody's seen anything

419
00:26:49,719 --> 00:26:54,589
空を見ても 見えない夜の 欠けた月に
Even looking at the sky, in the unseen night, at the waning moon

420
00:26:55,199 --> 00:26:57,749
嘘に 嘘に 嘘に
Lies, lies, lies

421
00:26:58,299 --> 00:27:00,769
これはなんだ それは何処
What is this? Where is that?

422
00:27:00,769 --> 00:27:04,319
ここは魂 それでよろし
This is the soul, and that's just fine

423
00:27:05,199 --> 00:27:07,819
走る 逃げる 見なす
Run, escape, look away

424
00:27:08,529 --> 00:27:11,949
月の 欠けた 場所へ
To the place where the moon is waning

425
00:27:26,409 --> 00:27:29,909
もう3番目ならなく
If it's already the third one, it doesn't ring

426
00:27:29,909 --> 00:27:36,659
さぁ咎めなく 衝動おさまらず
Come now, without blame, the impulse cannot be contained

427
00:27:37,169 --> 00:27:40,579
なぜか なぜか 知らぬ
Why, why, I don't know

428
00:27:40,579 --> 00:27:44,479
最悪だ 五臓六腑を吐いて濡れ踊れ
It's the worst, throw up your insides and dance wetly

429
00:27:44,479 --> 00:27:47,979
嘘ついてが なんねなんでつってなんか
Telling lies, why why saying something something

430
00:27:48,429 --> 00:27:52,089
最悪だ どうもこうもしねぇよ勝手にしやがれ
It's the worst, do whatever you want, I don't care

431
00:27:52,089 --> 00:27:55,429
嘘ついてが やれも本当最悪だ
Telling lies, doing it is truly the worst

432
00:27:55,429 --> 00:28:02,229
寝ても覚めても突き纏う 見える意思きの裏側に
Whether sleeping or waking, it clings, on the flip side of visible intent

433
00:28:02,229 --> 00:28:08,619
大きく開く黒い穴 分かり 分かる 分かる
A huge opening black hole, I understand, I understand, I understand

434
00:28:09,229 --> 00:28:12,849
許す 許せぬ 許す 許せぬ
Forgive, unforgivable, forgive, unforgivable

435
00:28:13,209 --> 00:28:15,619
かわいい 怖い
Cute, scary

436
00:28:16,239 --> 00:28:22,119
リンゴ ゴリラ ラクダ ゴリラ ラクダ ラボラ ラマダン
Apple, gorilla, camel, gorilla, camel, laboratory, Ramadan

437
00:28:37,989 --> 00:28:44,319
私たち 絶対に見てません 知ってません 聞いてません 知ったこっちゃありません
We definitely didn't see anything, don't know, didn't hear, none of our business

438
00:28:44,699 --> 00:28:52,599
視界を一石二鳥に一つ 許さるざる思考をあざ笑うように 包んで生きていこうじゃありませんか
Let's wrap up and live on, mocking thoughts that cannot be forgiven, all in one fell swoop

439
00:28:53,789 --> 00:28:56,689
孤独など持たず
Without holding onto things like loneliness

440
00:28:57,289 --> 00:29:03,639
今日さえ意味もなく 映画館に満足
Today too, meaninglessly satisfied at the cinema

441
00:29:04,189 --> 00:29:09,269
だから だから だから 最高だ
Therefore, therefore, therefore, it's the best

442
00:29:09,869 --> 00:29:13,409
脳がこうかしてんだぶっ壊して叫べ
My brain is hallucinating like this, smash it and shout

443
00:29:13,409 --> 00:29:17,479
最悪だ なんねなんでつってまこまこ離れて最高だ
It's the worst, saying why why, separating completely, it's the best

444
00:29:17,479 --> 00:29:20,539
鼓膜でけっこう勝手に生き足れ
Living however you like with your eardrums

445
00:29:20,539 --> 00:29:24,179
最悪だ やれも本当最高だ
It's the worst, doing it is truly the best

446
00:29:24,479 --> 00:29:31,079
昔々のおまいら 向き向き身のひとだから
You guys from long ago, you're the kind of people who...

447
00:29:31,489 --> 00:29:37,449
無際無限の生まれ月 それが それが それが
The birth month of infinite boundaries, that is, that is, that is

448
00:29:37,879 --> 00:29:45,409
無関心に押し寄せる あんたもあたしも関係ない 無関心に押し寄せる 楽しくやってりゃもう満点
Crushing in with indifference, you and I have nothing to do with it. Crushing in with indifference, if you're having fun, that's already a 10/10

449
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:52,849
勝手にやってりゃ問題なし それは知らない 何も知らない 何もいない 何も
No problem if you do it on your own. I don't know that, I know nothing, nobody is there, nothing

450
00:29:52,849 --> 00:29:59,994
聞けない 何も言えない
Can't hear, can't say anything

451
00:30:00,191 --> 00:30:01,421
うわつく甘い街の喧騒
Due to the hustle and bustle of a sweet, floating city,

452
00:30:01,421 --> 00:30:03,481
故に感情線は渋滞
the emotional lines got congested.

453
00:30:03,481 --> 00:30:05,181
「僕に関係ない」とか言って
After saying, "That doesn't concern me,"

454
00:30:05,181 --> 00:30:07,521
心模様 白く染まって
my heart pattern is dyed white.

455
00:30:16,368 --> 00:30:20,668
超的な力が殺人事件に関わっている？
A supernatural occurrence, happening in a murder case?

456
00:30:20,808 --> 00:30:24,548
いやいやそんな、ねぇ？
That's just unbelievable.

457
00:30:25,178 --> 00:30:31,218
にわかには信じがたいが、今の手がかりから推理するとそういうことになる。
She had a hard time believing it, but all the hints said otherwise.

458
00:30:31,928 --> 00:30:37,648
まだパズルのピースがピタリとはまらないこの不思議で奇妙な事件。
Still, there were pieces of this puzzle that refused to fit,

459
00:30:38,118 --> 00:30:42,598
探偵は信頼できる情報源に頼ることにした。
so the detective turned to a reliable source for help.

460
00:30:44,278 --> 00:30:45,418
あっ、来てくれたー
Hey, I'm glad—

461
00:30:46,148 --> 00:30:49,108
…なんで君達まで？
—And why are you guys also here?

462
00:30:49,958 --> 00:30:52,958
ゼータが来るって聞いたから、アーニャにちょっかいかけてやろうと思って！
We heard Zeta was coming over, and decided to bug ya!

463
00:30:53,378 --> 00:30:54,748
はいはい。
Yes, yes, I see.

464
00:30:55,278 --> 00:30:56,628
もー！つれないなぁ。
Aww, come on!

465
00:30:57,038 --> 00:30:59,928
それはそうと…ゼータ、何かつかめた？
Anyway, Zeta, did you find anything?

466
00:31:00,098 --> 00:31:03,978
もちろん！優秀なシークレットエージェントなので！
Of course! I'm not an elite secret agent for nothing.

467
00:31:04,358 --> 00:31:11,308
イナの描いた似顔絵と大空警察の資料から、被害者の身元を特定できたよ。
Between the portrait from Ina and the files from the Oozora Police, I've been able to positively ID the murder victim.

468
00:31:11,308 --> 00:31:14,438
でも…ちょっと変なんだよね。
But... what I found is weird.

469
00:31:14,438 --> 00:31:15,078
変？
How so?

470
00:31:15,428 --> 00:31:20,069
被害者の履歴を調べたところ、その人物は何百年も前の時代の人だったんだ。
Well, when I investigated their history, I found that they actually lived centuries ago.

471
00:31:20,069 --> 00:31:25,638
でもその人物が、数日前になぜか死体で発見された…話がつながらないんだよ。
So how they were also somehow murdered just days ago... it doesn't make any sense.

472
00:31:26,248 --> 00:31:29,818
アーニャからもらった情報に間違いがあったとか？
Did you perhaps confuse your information? Or...

473
00:31:30,228 --> 00:31:34,308
なるほど、やっとつながってきた。
Actually, things are finally starting to make sense.

474
00:31:34,978 --> 00:31:37,458
一人の被害者が、過去と現在で二度死んだことになる。
A victim caught between two times.

475
00:31:37,828 --> 00:31:40,528
誰かが時間と次元をねじ曲げて、そんな状況を作り出した。
One who died in two different ways.

476
00:31:41,128 --> 00:31:46,408
なかなかできることじゃない…
Not many exist who can cause time and dimensions to warp in a way to make that possible...

477
00:31:46,958 --> 00:31:49,848
でも君なら可能でしょ。
...but you're one of them.

478
00:31:50,888 --> 00:31:52,358
さすがは名探偵。
Well done, detective.

479
00:31:52,958 --> 00:31:56,069
ちょっと時間がかかりすぎかな。
Took you long enough.

480
00:31:56,069 --> 00:31:56,958
危うくネタばらしするとこだった。
I was this close to telling ya the whole thing.

481
00:31:56,958 --> 00:31:59,958
レイネが書いてくれた、この匿名の手紙もいいヒントになったよ。
You helped enough with this "anonymous" letter about the murder.

482
00:32:00,169 --> 00:32:02,208
えっ、バレてた？
O-oh, you figured out that was me?

483
00:32:02,428 --> 00:32:04,548
書き方のクセで分かる。
I recognized your writing style.

484
00:32:04,988 --> 00:32:09,598
待って、どういうこと？ムーナと被害者にどんな関係があるの？
W-wait, I don't get it. What does Moona have to do with the victim?

485
00:32:10,118 --> 00:32:14,878
ムーナは、別の時空で殺された遺体を我々がいるこの時空へ移動させたんだ。
She took a murder victim from another space and time, and moved them into our dimension.

486
00:32:15,098 --> 00:32:18,968
ゼータが特定した人物は、この世界線における同人物ってこと。
The one you IDed was this universe's version of the same person.

487
00:32:19,278 --> 00:32:23,588
えー、おっけー。でもどうしてそんなことを？
Uh... okay. But then why?

488
00:32:23,938 --> 00:32:29,938
理由も気になるけど、それより確かめたいことがある。
That is an important question, but there's one I want answered even more.

489
00:32:30,418 --> 00:32:33,478
ムーナが…私にあの夢を見せたの？
Are you... responsible for my dreams?

490
00:32:33,798 --> 00:32:35,108
それは違う。
No.

491
00:32:35,868 --> 00:32:44,548
あなたがあの夢を見ていることを知って、私はあの夢が生まれる根源を調べてみた。そして見つけたのが、次元の向こう側から声を届けようとする魂。
After I learned about your dreams, I used my powers to search for the source of them. I found a spirit reaching out from time and dimensions.

492
00:32:45,048 --> 00:32:48,958
私はその魂のために橋渡しをしてあげただけ…。
All I've done is try to help them by making the bridge a little easier...

493
00:32:49,069 --> 00:32:52,618
私も手伝ったよ！というか、私のアイデア。
With my help! I mean, it was my idea...

494
00:32:52,998 --> 00:32:54,098
そう。
True.

495
00:32:54,758 --> 00:33:04,418
ただやり方が悪かったのか、アーニャの見たものが他の人にも見えちゃったみたい。巻き込んだKFPの従業員には後でお詫びしなきゃ…。
Though doing it this way has caused some of what you've been experiencing to leak to other people. We're going to have to apologize to the KFP workers...

496
00:33:05,068 --> 00:33:08,488
でもその魂が、どうして私に声を届けようとしてるの？
But why is the spirit reaching out to me of all people?

497
00:33:08,958 --> 00:33:13,508
それは私に訊くことじゃないない。私が話すべきことじゃない。
It wouldn't be right for me to answer those questions. It's not my story to tell.

498
00:33:13,958 --> 00:33:17,458
あの魂に心を開いてあげて。それだけでいい。
Open yourself up to the spirits, and they'll do the rest.

499
00:33:17,908 --> 00:33:20,988
心をもっと開く方法なら知ってるよ！
I got a way to make yourself more open to spirits!

500
00:33:21,208 --> 00:33:22,468
それって歌？
Is it through song?

501
00:33:22,758 --> 00:33:24,548
え？なんで分かったの？
Huh? How'd you know?

502
00:33:24,888 --> 00:33:26,618
まあ、勘かな…。
Lucky guess...

503
00:33:55,297 --> 00:34:00,057
想い出してた 想い出の中で泣いてた
I was remembering, crying inside my memories.

504
00:34:00,117 --> 00:34:05,227
確かめたい夢と孤独を抱えて笑ってた
I was smiling, embracing the dreams and loneliness I wanted to verify.

505
00:34:05,657 --> 00:34:10,587
この痛みもキスも拭えないドミノに見返してしまいそうな
This pain and these kisses might make me retaliate against the inescapable dominoes,

506
00:34:10,817 --> 00:34:15,607
焦りとか不安が滲んで涙にのまれてしまう
as impatience and anxiety seep in and swallow me in tears.

507
00:34:16,217 --> 00:34:20,807
誰ひとりかけることはないライトニンググラデーション
A lightning gradation where no one is missing.

508
00:34:21,069 --> 00:34:26,569
僕らの想いが音になって繋ぐ こだまさせて
Let our feelings turn into sound and connect, making it echo.

509
00:34:26,669 --> 00:34:31,969
忘れないよ 隠したシークレットライフを
I won't forget the hidden secret life.

510
00:34:32,169 --> 00:34:37,369
あの日僕らは間違いだって取ったんだ としる
That day, we knew we had made a mistake.

511
00:34:37,369 --> 00:34:42,569
飛ばしてしまい この愛しさを 何度も探し出して
Skip it all and keep searching for this preciousness over and over.

512
00:34:42,569 --> 00:34:48,569
君の声を光らせて ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
Make your voice shine and scream that you're here.

513
00:34:48,569 --> 00:34:52,569
その手を離さないで
Don't let go of that hand.

514
00:34:56,569 --> 00:35:01,419
世界に僕だけが取り残されてしま
I was left behind alone in this world...

515
00:35:00,163 --> 00:35:01,413
SNS午前2時
SNS at 2:00 AM,

516
00:35:01,517 --> 00:35:03,217
深夜のアスファルト 裸足で立つ
standing barefoot on the midnight asphalt.

517
00:35:03,317 --> 00:35:06,217
立ち止まり 手放してしまうなら
If I stopped and let go of it all,

518
00:35:06,917 --> 00:35:11,617
心が通じ合えないなら 黒髪を絞り殺してしまうなら
If our hearts can't connect, if we're going to strangle our dark hair...

519
00:35:12,117 --> 00:35:16,917
一人でいたほうが楽に生きられたのかな
Would it have been easier to live alone?

520
00:35:17,117 --> 00:35:22,617
憧れ理想に強く惹かれる 感情が
Emotions strongly drawn to longing and ideals

521
00:35:22,617 --> 00:35:26,617
僕らを巻き込んでしまうのなら
If they're going to sweep us up,

522
00:35:26,617 --> 00:35:29,617
答えて
give us an answer!

523
00:35:37,617 --> 00:35:44,917
狂わせて いく まだ 笑っていたいんだ ぼくらの延長線上の
Drive me mad, I still want to smile, on our extension line

524
00:35:45,117 --> 00:35:49,117
この音が途切れるまで
until this sound cuts off.

525
00:35:49,617 --> 00:35:53,617
孤独の心に描いた色
The color drawn in a lonely heart,

526
00:35:54,117 --> 00:35:58,117
君の出番が待ってる
your turn is waiting.

527
00:36:00,117 --> 00:36:03,917
狂わせて 忘れないよう 鍵鳴らすタイミングを
Drive me mad, so I won't forget, the timing of unlocking the key.

528
00:36:04,117 --> 00:36:09,117
あの時ぼくらは巻き込まれていなかったと知る
Realizing that back then we weren't even involved,

529
00:36:09,617 --> 00:36:14,617
閉ざして しまい込んだ 一線の光探して
searching for a single ray of light shut away inside.

530
00:36:15,117 --> 00:36:18,617
君の声を聴かせて
Let me hear your voice,

531
00:36:18,617 --> 00:36:22,117
ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
shout out that you're here!

532
00:36:22,117 --> 00:36:27,617
その手を離さないで
Don't let go of that hand.

533
00:36:39,163 --> 00:36:43,817
魂に心を向け？簡単に言ってくれる。
Opening up your heart to the soul? Easy for you to say.

534
00:36:44,873 --> 00:36:53,417
探偵になる前の彼女の人生において、他者に心を開くのは危険な行為だった。
In her life before becoming a detective, opening up to someone was dangerous.

535
00:36:54,217 --> 00:36:56,617
今でもその本能は変わらない。
That instinct still lingers.

536
00:37:00,117 --> 00:37:02,617
結局何も進展はなかった。
This was getting her nowhere.

537
00:37:03,117 --> 00:37:09,117
謎はまだ残っているが、彼女はここのところ無理が続いていた。
She still had questions she needed answered, but maybe she had wound herself up too much.

538
00:37:13,617 --> 00:37:16,117
少し休まなければ。
She needed a break.

539
00:37:25,249 --> 00:37:34,117
Hello, everyone! I'm Hatsune Miku, a virtual idol. Well, that's what everyone seems to think, but secretly, I'm -
Hello, everyone! I'm Hatsune Miku, a virtual idol. Well, that's what everyone seems to think, but secretly, I'm—

540
00:37:44,917 --> 00:37:47,417
I wake up to a call, put my frilly outfit on now

541
00:37:47,417 --> 00:37:49,917
It's time I open up my eyes and start the day

542
00:37:49,917 --> 00:37:52,317
I combat 'til the dawn, until every villain's gone, yeah!

543
00:37:52,317 --> 00:37:55,117
A clumsy trip, and now I've fallen to my butt

544
00:37:55,117 --> 00:37:57,617
With my magical phone and a silly little ringtone

545
00:37:57,617 --> 00:38:00,117
I'll shout a magic word and set the world in place

546
00:38:00,117 --> 00:38:02,917
Whatever it may cost, there's no reason to stop

547
00:38:02,917 --> 00:38:04,917
For a world that I cherish and love

548
00:38:04,917 --> 00:38:07,617
Monsters might be a scary foe to fight

549
00:38:07,617 --> 00:38:09,617
But I'll take the stand

550
00:38:09,617 --> 00:38:12,617
If I can stop your tears and wipe them dry

551
00:38:12,617 --> 00:38:15,117
If my pain's a type of cure for peace, I don't mind

552
00:38:15,117 --> 00:38:17,617
I can play as a nurse healing you every day

553
00:38:17,617 --> 00:38:20,117
So what if I might shed a tear, get some bruises?

554
00:38:20,117 --> 00:38:24,617
A wipe is all I need to clean the cherry blush away, ha!

555
00:38:24,617 --> 00:38:27,617
Fighting through the night, but I'm wide awake

556
00:38:27,617 --> 00:38:29,917
It can all be so hard for me to get through the day

557
00:38:29,917 --> 00:38:32,317
Your smile is enough to heal all my aches

558
00:38:32,317 --> 00:38:34,617
Wrapped in a cute band-aid

559
00:38:34,617 --> 00:38:39,617
I can take the pain, fight all day, fill up the syringe with love, heal up the world and go again

560
00:38:50,117 --> 00:38:55,117
And now it's time for the moment you've been waiting for!

561
00:38:55,117 --> 00:38:58,117
One, two, three, ready? Miku, miku beam!

562
00:39:09,117 --> 00:39:11,617
On my own, without anyone to know

563
00:39:11,617 --> 00:39:14,317
How my job's not all rainbows

564
00:39:14,317 --> 00:39:17,117
But then I think about your smile

565
00:39:17,117 --> 00:39:19,617
I'm a magically bright invincible girl

566
00:39:19,617 --> 00:39:22,617
If you need me to heal, go on and call out my name

567
00:39:22,617 --> 00:39:25,117
When you find yourself going down a spiral

568
00:39:25,117 --> 00:39:29,617
I'll bonk away what puts you down, a pink hammer melee, ya!

569
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:33,117
Fighting through the night, but I'm wide awake

570
00:39:33,117 --> 00:39:35,117
All alone, it's so hard for me to get through the rain

571
00:39:35,117 --> 00:39:37,117
Your smile is enough to make my day

572
00:39:37,117 --> 00:39:39,617
So I stand tall and brave

573
00:39:39,617 --> 00:39:44,617
'Cause I'm not afraid, any pain, I can laugh away, chin up, with love, I'll fight on 'til the end

574
00:39:50,117 --> 00:39:52,617
A a, nemui yo ~
Ah, I'm sleepy~

575
00:40:05,014 --> 00:40:08,234
Bearing through the pain, I try to be brave

576
00:40:09,614 --> 00:40:12,874
As long as you can stay happy, I'm okay

577
00:40:13,574 --> 00:40:17,474
I'm not gonna bend, ha! I can be a cure for peace in your heart
I'm not gonna bend! I can be a cure for peace in your heart,

578
00:40:17,474 --> 00:40:22,074
and play as a nurse healing you every day. Your smile is enough to heal all my aches

579
00:40:22,074 --> 00:40:24,574
all in a cute band-aid

580
00:40:24,574 --> 00:40:29,874
If you're feeling pain, call my name, I'll be by your side 'til I see your smile beam bright again

581
00:40:29,934 --> 00:40:34,594
うりゃおい！うりゃおい！う～ファイター！ スーパーパワフルミクちゃーん！
Urya oi! Urya oi! Super powerful Miku-chan!

582
00:40:35,114 --> 00:40:39,474
うりゃおい！うりゃおい！う～サイバー！ミクミクミク GO！
Urya oi! Urya oi! Miku Miku Miku go!

583
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:45,092
あぁ、眠いよ…
Ah, I'm so sleepy...

584
00:41:00,914 --> 00:41:04,194
ユメ…だった…？
It was a dream...?

585
00:42:52,292 --> 00:42:58,592
知った。救いのかない形だった、僕の声は
I realized. It was a form without salvation, my voice—

586
00:42:58,892 --> 00:43:05,092
知った。救いのかない赤い血が流れてんだ
I realized. Unsalvageable red blood is flowing.

587
00:43:05,592 --> 00:43:12,192
たらたら遅い来る影ばかり 道で喧嘩すること真上に上がれないよ風
Dripping shadows slow to arrive, fighting on the road, the wind can't rise straight up.

588
00:43:12,392 --> 00:43:18,892
赤く光る場所へ 裸足でかけたら ただ膝をかかえている君がいただから
Running barefoot to a glowing red place, there you were hugging your knees, so—

589
00:43:19,492 --> 00:43:25,592
ENCOUNT! 悲劇ぶった天国へ
ENCOUNT! To a heaven playing at tragedy,

590
00:43:25,992 --> 00:43:32,092
不甲斐ない瞳きっとあのひみつみつめた君のせいだ
cowardly eyes, surely, staring at that secret was your fault.

591
00:43:32,492 --> 00:43:40,092
はやく はやく 身を揺らして 遠い遠い 水面の向こうへと
Hurry, hurry, shake your body, far, far across the water's surface...

592
00:44:02,192 --> 00:44:08,092
知った。救いのかない熱を持った、僕の円環
I realized. My circle, holding unredeemable heat—

593
00:44:09,192 --> 00:44:13,892
知った。潤いのない君の目は見にくかった
I realized. Your moistureless eyes were hard to look at.

594
00:44:14,292 --> 00:44:28,092
酷く 酷く 酷く...
Cruel, cruel, cruel...

595
00:44:42,192 --> 00:44:51,592
汚染としてるその顔に触れてみたかった
I wanted to touch that contaminated face.

596
00:44:54,992 --> 00:45:00,092
ENCOUNT! 悲劇ぶった天国へ
ENCOUNT! To a heaven playing at tragedy...

597
00:45:01,540 --> 00:45:02,240
知ってた
I knew it.

598
00:45:02,240 --> 00:45:03,340
救いのない形だった僕の声は
My voice was a form with no salvation,

599
00:45:03,340 --> 00:45:04,340
散った
scattered,

600
00:45:04,340 --> 00:45:06,118
狂いのない赤い血が流れているんだ
and crimson blood without madness flows.

601
00:45:07,268 --> 00:45:07,868
ただただ襲い来る影ばかり満ちてて掠う言葉たちあがれない夜風灼かるひかる地獄へ裸足で駆けたらただ膝を抱えている貴方がいた
You, who were just holding your knees, were there.

602
00:45:08,118 --> 00:45:08,718
だから encounter！悲劇ぶった天国へ
So, encounter! To a heaven that ruined tragedy,

603
00:45:08,718 --> 00:45:09,318
“いつか嫌って僕を嫌って”
"Someday, hate me, hate me,"

604
00:45:09,318 --> 00:45:09,918
不甲斐ない瞳きっと、
pitiful eyes, surely,

605
00:45:09,918 --> 00:45:10,718
あの日みつめた貴方のせいだ
it's because of you, whom I gazed at that day.

606
00:45:14,518 --> 00:45:15,318
“背を向けた”はやく身を委ねて？淡々水面のむこうへと
"Turned your back." Hurry, surrender your body to the other side of the pale, pale water surface?

607
00:45:16,718 --> 00:45:17,518
“視線違う”知った、救いのない熱を持った僕の炎夏
"Gaze differs." I knew it, my scorching summer with a heat that had no salvation.

608
00:45:19,518 --> 00:45:20,318
散った、憂いのない貴方の瞳は、醜く酷く
Scattered, your eyes with no melancholy were ugly, horribly so.

609
00:45:29,367 --> 00:45:29,967
“強く”
"Strongly"

610
00:45:31,567 --> 00:45:32,567
茫然としているその表情に触れてみたかった
I wanted to touch that bewildered expression.

611
00:45:35,367 --> 00:45:35,967
だから encounter！喜劇ぶった天国へ
So, encounter! To a heaven that faked a comedy,

612
